nging the record's gender identity \"without written parental consent\".\n- **Why no chair:** the bill acts on the education record, not on staff using a different name or pronouns, so it does not meet rung 5. It does not require schools to notify parents, so it does not meet rung 4. And it goes further than handing information over when parents ask, so rung 3 does not fit either. It shows which side he is on, but no single rung matches every clause.\n- **Passages:** I coded the vote page and the bill text as one vote record. The vote page carries his name as printed (`Cullimore, K. A.`) and the count (`Yeas 22 Nays 6 Abs 1`). The bill text carries the provision quote.\n- **One assumption:** his term dates are given as unknown. I coded the 2023 vote as `in-term` on the basis that it is a Senate vote; code will need to confirm his term covers it.\n\n`rests_on` and `needs_source` are empty, and there are no quotes to tier.","ttft_ms":14499,"type":"result","duration_ms":32576,"uuid":"ec520adb-8468-4ec5-b435-14c321b50c3b","ttft_stream_ms":7505,"time_to_request_ms":303,"first_content_frame_ms":7505,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
